<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-response-time> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-response-time> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hygromorph response time scales as thickness squared" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-response-time> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The time a hygromorphic bilayer takes to respond to a change in ambient humidity is set by diffusion of water through its thickness, so it grows as the square of the thickness divided by the diffusion coefficient." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-response-time> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-response-time> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "\\tau \\sim h^2 / D" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-response-time> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: water transport through the layer is Fickian diffusion with constant diffusivity D; the mechanical response is quasi-static (elastic relaxation much faster than diffusion); a single dominant thickness h. Formal status: proved as the diffusive time scale of the one-dimensional diffusion equation (the slowest mode decays as exp(-pi^2 D t / h^2) for a layer of thickness h with fixed boundary concentration). Reyssat and Mahadevan (2009) measured tau against h for paper–polymer bilayers and pine cone scales and found the quadratic scaling. Non-Fickian sorption, swelling-dependent D and internal cavities change the exponent." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-response-time> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Record the opening-angle time series of pine cone scales (or bilayers) of several thicknesses after a humidity step, fit an exponential time constant to each, and regress log(tau) on log(h); pass if the slope is 2 within its confidence interval." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-response-time> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-response-time> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Etienne Reyssat & L. Mahadevan (2009) Hygromorphs: from pine cones to biomimetic bilayers" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hygromorph-response-time> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1038/37745> .
}
